  "abstract": "Whether a rational Diophantine septuple exists remains open. We study strong members, whose square plus one is a square, in the three fixed square-product quintuple families of Dujella, Kazalicki and Petričević. Earlier work excluded fourteen of their fifteen coordinate cases. We prove that the remaining case contributes at most one nondegenerate quintuple up to global negation and reordering, represented by at most four rational parameters. An all-bad-prime point-class sieve fixes an elliptic twist over a quartic field. Its rank is at most three, although only two independent points are known. We control the entire projective pencil of annihilators of these logarithms. At seven, the elementary square conditions leave one parameter disk. The first two projected Taylor coefficient vectors dominate every higher coefficient, and an infinite-tail estimate gives at most two zeros uniformly by Strassmann’s theorem. Removing a known inadmissible zero and applying a free Klein-four symmetry proves the count bound without a complete Mordell–Weil group. Separately, exact duplication identities and rigorous height intervals certify a complete basis for the rational quartic’s elliptic Jacobian. A complete local sieve of 400,040,001 coefficient pairs then proves that any remaining family parameter has a reduced numerator or denominator with more than 1,350,000 decimal digits. A source-only supplement reproduces both results in seventeen stages. These are unconditional bounds for the named families; they neither establish existence nor exclude the last coordinate, and do not resolve arbitrary rational Diophantine septuples.",
